    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d16-a1">

                <pb facs="0120" n="20" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg20"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Governor Pattison to Mr. Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harrisburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-09-05"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 5,
                        1884</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor herewith to transmit to
                    you the reply of the Hon. A. Fulton, mayor of the city of Pittsburgh, Pa., in
                    relation to the alleged insult offered by the chief of the police force of that
                    city to the representative of the Austrian Government and its flag. In this
                    reply you will observe that your favor of the 28th ultimo to me on the same
                    subject was laid before his honor Mayor Fulton.</p>
                <p>Awaiting your further pleasure in the matter,</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ROBT. E. PATTISON,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Governor.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
